tests/selftest — the oracle-selftest loop's corpus and banked findings

Driver: tools/oracle-selftest.sh. Run it from the repo root:

  bash tools/oracle-selftest.sh                 # against pinned boot (default)
  bash tools/oracle-selftest.sh --compiler PATH # against a fresh wt_m2_ensure m2.wasm

The medium is its own test generator (PLAN §11 col 2). This v1 drives the Synth proposer
through the `edit`/address transport: each skeleton is a complete program with
one authored `??` in a typed position; the loop runs `edit` non-interactively
(printf 'y\n' accepts the top survivor), then compiles / assembles / runs
whatever the medium proposed and classifies the result. A trap or a
non-assemblable emit is a banked crucible, not a loop failure — the loop found a
real gap. We bank, we do not fix compiler code here.

skeletons/ — the input corpus. Each carries `// selftest-shape:` and `// selftest-expect:`
directives (self-describing; the loop reads them for the results TSV and the
regression/graduation check). Six skeletons over five type shapes:

  s01_int_refinement   Int hole under a refinement        -> clean-run (exit 1)
  s02_float_arith      Float hole in arithmetic           -> edit-trap
  s03_list_elem        Int hole in a list element         -> edit-trap
  s04_effect_row       hole under a !Network row           -> clean-run (exit 7)
  s05_arg_float        hole as a fn argument              -> assemble-fail
  s06_div_zero         hole refined to a runtime hazard    -> runtime-trap

crucibles/ — the banked findings, regenerated every run (a graduated finding
leaves the dir; a fresh one enters). Each holds the reproducer .mn, the relevant
artifact (backtrace / rejected .wat / shrunk repro), and a README with the exact
reproduce command. Text-only: the raw trapping .wasm is regenerable from the .mn
and never committed as a binary.

Classes: clean-run and refuse-unfilled are correct behavior (not banked).
edit-trap / compile-error / assemble-fail / runtime-trap are findings (banked).
A runtime-trap additionally runs `wasm-tools shrink` to bank a minimal repro.

Current findings against boot (four, all distinct):
  s02  the Propose facet traps enumerating float candidates
       (indirect call type mismatch in enumerate_float_literals — the open
       Hbeta.emit.float-evidence-ft class, PLAN §7 residue).
  s03  projecting the cursor over a list-bearing program traps in inference
       (region_bucket_scan -> list_index, `unreachable`).
  s05  a Float-returning main threads f64 through the i32 `_start` boundary;
       wat2wasm rejects the emit.
  s06  a proven fill (`0`, the only inhabitant of `Int where self == 0`) builds
       a program that divides by it and traps at runtime — proof is a filter over
       admissible values, not a guarantee about the program they build (PLAN §1).

Residue (v1): program SHAPE is hand-authored. The loop varies programs only
through the medium's own hole-proposals over these fixed skeletons. Whole-program
(decl-level) generation waits on a real `enumerate_inhabitants` driver; when it
lands, this corpus becomes its seed set.
